# What each tool does: its tooltip, and the status line while it is pointed at. A tooltip's
# key is `tooltip-` and the tool's id, as its name's is `tools-` and its id.

tooltip-create-shape-round = Create Shape, Round: raises the selected closed vectors into a 3D dome that rises at the angle you set and rounds over the top
tooltip-create-shape-angled = Create Shape, Angled: raises the selected closed vectors into a 3D shape with straight slopes, like a roof or a pyramid
tooltip-create-shape-smooth = Create Shape, Smooth: raises the selected closed vectors into a 3D shape whose sides curve gently up out of the edge and over the top
tooltip-create-shape-flat = Create Shape, Flat: raises the selected closed vectors into a flat-topped 3D shape, all one height, like a plateau
tooltip-edit-text = Edit Text: opens the selected text in its form, to change its words, font or size (text in a group too); double-clicking the text does the same
tooltip-align-left = Align Left: moves the selected objects sideways so their left edges line up with the selection's left edge
tooltip-align-right = Align Right: moves the selected objects sideways so their right edges line up with the selection's right edge
tooltip-align-top = Align Top: moves the selected objects up or down so their top edges line up with the selection's top
tooltip-align-bottom = Align Bottom: moves the selected objects up or down so their bottom edges line up with the selection's bottom
tooltip-center-horizontally = Center Horizontally: moves the selected objects sideways so their centres line up on one vertical line. A group, like a word of text, moves as one piece
tooltip-center-vertically = Center Vertically: moves the selected objects up or down so their centres line up on one horizontal line. A group, like a word of text, moves as one piece
tooltip-center = Center: moves the selected objects so their centres all sit on one point, the middle of the selection. A group, like a word of text, moves as one piece
tooltip-center-horizontally-in-material = Center Horizontally in Material: moves the selection sideways to the middle of the material's width
tooltip-center-vertically-in-material = Center Vertically in Material: moves the selection up or down to the middle of the material's height
tooltip-center-in-material = Center in Material: moves the selection to the very middle of the material
tooltip-select-all-vectors = Select All Vectors: selects every vector on the layers that are shown and not locked
tooltip-select-all-open-vectors = Select All Open Vectors: selects every vector whose ends do not meet, often the ones a toolpath cannot use
tooltip-select-all-duplicate-vectors = Select All Duplicate Vectors: selects the extra copies of vectors drawn exactly on top of others, so you can delete them and keep one of each
tooltip-select-vectors-inside = Select Vectors Inside: adds every vector that lies wholly inside a selected closed shape, so a part with its holes is picked in one go
tooltip-span-to-line = Convert Span to Line: makes the span under the pointer a straight line between its two nodes
tooltip-span-to-arc = Convert Span to Arc: makes the span under the pointer a circular arc between its two nodes
tooltip-span-to-bezier = Convert Span to Bezier: makes the span under the pointer a curve with two handles you can drag to shape it
tooltip-move-node = Move Node: drags the node (a square) under the pointer to a new place; a curve's handles move with it
tooltip-move-handle = Move Handle: drags a curve's round handle in Node Edit to bend that span; its nodes stay put
tooltip-ungroup-onto-current-layer = Ungroup onto Current Layer: takes the selected groups apart one level (groups and text in them come out as they were) and moves their vectors onto the layer you are working on
tooltip-merge-visible-layers = Merge Visible: moves the vectors of every shown, unlocked layer onto this one. This layer is shown and unlocked so the merged work can be edited; locked layers are left as they are
tooltip-group-toolpaths = Group Toolpaths: puts the selected toolpaths together in a folder in the toolpath list, to keep a long list tidy. A folder can hold folders of its own
tooltip-arrange-toolpaths = Arrange Toolpaths: puts the toolpaths in a new cutting order, and in or out of groups, in one step, as dragging them (or whole groups) in the toolpath list does
tooltip-show-toolpath-group = Show or Hide Toolpath Group: the tick beside a group's name shows or hides every toolpath in it, its sub-groups' too, in one step
tooltip-rename-toolpath-group = Rename Toolpath Group: gives a folder of toolpaths a new name
tooltip-ungroup-toolpaths = Ungroup Toolpaths: takes a folder apart one level, its toolpaths and folders moving up into the folder it sat in, or deletes them with it
tooltip-ungroup-merged-toolpath = Ungroup Merged Toolpath: splits a merged toolpath back into the toolpaths it was made from
tooltip-break-text-into-lines = Break Block into Lines: splits a block of text into one text object per line, so each line can be moved on its own
tooltip-make-real-line = Make Real Line: turns the selected dashed construction lines back into normal vectors, so toolpaths can cut them and exported files include them
tooltip-unselect-all = Unselect All: clears the selection, so nothing is picked and no tool will change anything until you pick again
tooltip-select = Select: puts away the tool in hand, so clicking picks objects, Shift-click adds to the pick, dragging draws a box round them (a slip of a pixel or two is still a click, not a move), and right-clicking an object picks it and opens its menu
tooltip-transform = Transform: click an object to move, size or rotate it with handles you drag; click it again to switch between sizing and rotating
tooltip-node-edit = Node Edit: shows the points (nodes) a vector is made of, to drag them, or right-click to add, delete or change them. Del deletes the nodes picked with a box; picked nodes are let go when you pick another vector, undo or leave Node Edit
tooltip-measure-inspect = Measure: drag between two points to read the distance and angle between them (both ends snap to ends, middles and centres as drawing does; hold Shift to place them freely), or click an object to see its size
tooltip-pan = Pan: drag the 2D view to slide the drawing round, without changing how close you are
tooltip-zoom-box = Zoom Box: drag a box round the part of the drawing you want to fill the view
tooltip-zoom-selected = Zoom Selected: zooms in or out until the selected objects fill the view
tooltip-zoom-to-drawing = Zoom to Drawing: fits everything you have drawn into the view, even what is off the material. In the 3D view F does it too, with the pointer over the view and no text box being typed in; F6 always does
tooltip-zoom-to-job = Zoom to Job: fits the whole material into the view
tooltip-refresh-2d-view = Refresh 2D View: draws the 2D view again from scratch
tooltip-new = New: starts a new job, asking the size and thickness of your material first
tooltip-new-from-template = New from Template: starts a new job from a saved template, with its material, vectors and toolpaths ready
tooltip-open = Open: opens a saved job to carry on with it
tooltip-close = Close: closes the job you have open, offering to save it first
tooltip-save = Save: saves the job under its own name, or asks for a name the first time
tooltip-save-as = Save As: saves the job under a new name or in another folder, starting from its own name and folder
tooltip-save-as-template = Save As Template: saves the job as a template, to start new jobs from it with the same material and toolpaths
tooltip-increment-and-save = Increment and Save: saves the job as a new copy with the next number on its name (sign_1, sign_2), keeping the earlier versions. A year or date on the end of the name stays as it is (Smith-2024 becomes Smith-2024_1, order_2024-11-15 becomes order_2024-11-15_1)
tooltip-recent-files = Recent Files: the jobs you opened last, to open one again
tooltip-exit = Exit: closes Cut Craft, offering to save your work first
tooltip-setup-material = Setup Material: sets this job's material: single sided, double sided or rotary, and its size
tooltip-open-folder = Open: opens a saved job, or a drawing or picture to bring in
tooltip-export-vectors = Export Vectors: saves the selected vectors as a drawing file (DXF, SVG and more) for another program
tooltip-export-dxf = Export as DXF: saves the selected vectors as a DXF file, which most drawing and CNC programs read
tooltip-export-svg = Export as SVG: saves the selected vectors as an SVG file, for laser cutters, vinyl cutters and drawing programs
tooltip-export-pdf = Export as PDF: saves the selected vectors as a PDF, to print or send
tooltip-export-eps = Export as EPS: saves the selected vectors as an EPS file, for older drawing and sign programs
tooltip-export-ai = Export as AI: saves the selected vectors as an Illustrator-style file, for drawing programs
tooltip-print = Print (opens a PDF): opens the 2D view as a PDF in your PDF viewer, to check and print from there
tooltip-save-shaded-image = Save Shaded Image: saves a picture of the 3D view, to show what the finished piece will look like
tooltip-save-toolpaths = Save Toolpaths: writes the toolpaths as a G-code file for your machine to run
tooltip-toolpath-summary = Toolpath Summary: lists every toolpath with its bit, depths and how long it takes to cut
tooltip-recalculate-all-toolpaths = Recalculate All Toolpaths: works out every toolpath again, after you changed the vectors or the material. A merged or copied toolpath is worked out after the toolpaths it copies
tooltip-tool-database = Bit Library: the list of your bits, with their sizes, speeds and feeds, to add, change or pick from. Renaming a bit renames it in this job's toolpaths too, and in other jobs when they open, so its tool changer slot still finds it
tooltip-tool-changer = Tool Changer (ATC): which bit is in each slot of your machine's automatic tool changer
tooltip-find-tool = Find Tool: type part of a tool's name to find it and open it, wherever it is in the menus
tooltip-undo = Undo: takes back the last change
tooltip-redo = Redo: puts back the change you just undid
tooltip-cut = Cut: removes the selected objects and keeps them on the clipboard, to paste somewhere else
tooltip-copy = Copy: puts a copy of the selected objects on the clipboard, to paste
tooltip-paste = Paste: adds the objects on the clipboard to the job exactly where they were copied from, on their own layer (in another job, on the current layer); a copied group or word of text pastes as a group of its own, still text (a dimension stays a dimension). Lines lying on top of their original show red. Ctrl+V of a copy made in another Cut Craft window brings its vectors only: 3D components paste only in the window they were copied in
tooltip-paste-in-place = Paste in Place: adds the objects on the clipboard to the job exactly where they were copied from; a copied group or word of text pastes as a group of its own
tooltip-edit-object = Edit Object: opens the selected object in the tool that made it, with its settings, to change them
tooltip-select-all-vectors-on-current-layer = Select All Vectors on Current Layer: selects every vector on the layer you are working on
tooltip-component-levels = Component Levels: opens the Components tab, where the 3D model's levels and components are listed. A new component goes on the level of the component picked there, else on the top shown level
tooltip-join-straight-line = Join with a Straight Line: joins the selected open vectors' nearest ends, or closes one, with a straight line
tooltip-join-smooth-curve = Join with a Smooth Curve: joins the selected open vectors' nearest ends, or closes one, with a curve that carries on smoothly
tooltip-join-move-end-points = Join by Moving End Points: moves the nearest ends of the selected open vectors to meet halfway, with no new line
tooltip-left-to-right = Space Left to Right: spreads the selected objects evenly across, in the order you picked them from the left; the outer ones stay put
tooltip-right-to-left = Space Right to Left: spreads the selected objects evenly across, in the order you picked them from the right; the outer ones stay put
tooltip-top-to-bottom = Space Top to Bottom: spreads the selected objects evenly up and down, in the order you picked them from the top; the outer ones stay put
tooltip-bottom-to-top = Space Bottom to Top: spreads the selected objects evenly up and down, in the order you picked them from the bottom; the outer ones stay put
tooltip-run-space-horizontally-order-left-to-right-inside-last-vector-false = Space Left to Right: spreads the selected objects evenly across, in the order you picked them from the left. A group, like a word of text, counts as one object
tooltip-run-space-horizontally-order-right-to-left-inside-last-vector-false = Space Right to Left: spreads the selected objects evenly across, in the order you picked them from the right. A group, like a word of text, counts as one object
tooltip-run-space-horizontally-order-as-placed-inside-last-vector-true = Space Horizontally Inside Last Vector: spreads the selected objects evenly across inside the vector you picked last
tooltip-run-space-vertically-order-top-to-bottom-inside-last-vector-false = Space Top to Bottom: spreads the selected objects evenly up and down, in the order you picked them from the top
tooltip-run-space-vertically-order-bottom-to-top-inside-last-vector-false = Space Bottom to Top: spreads the selected objects evenly up and down, in the order you picked them from the bottom
tooltip-run-space-vertically-order-as-placed-inside-last-vector-true = Space Vertically Inside Last Vector: spreads the selected objects evenly up and down inside the vector you picked last
tooltip-guides-visible = Guides Visible: shows or hides the guide lines you dragged out of the rulers; drag a guide where no shape lies on it to move it, or right-click it for its properties, to lock it or to delete it
tooltip-lock-all-existing-guides = Lock All Existing Guides: stops the guide lines from being moved by accident
tooltip-unlock-all-existing-guides = Unlock All Existing Guides: lets the guide lines be dragged again
tooltip-delete-all-guides = Delete All Guides: removes every guide line from the 2D view
tooltip-units-mm = Millimetres: shows and types sizes in millimetres
tooltip-units-inch = Inches: shows and types sizes in inches
tooltip-job-size-and-position = Job Size and Position: changes the material's size, thickness and where its origin is
tooltip-show-toolpaths-tab = Show Toolpaths Page: opens the Toolpaths page, where toolpaths are made and previewed
tooltip-interface-layout = Interface Layout: pick how the window is arranged: Ribbon, Rail, Canvas or Classic
tooltip-layout-classic = Classic Layout: the Design page on the left and the Toolpaths page on the right, opened from tabs at the sides
tooltip-layout-canvas = Canvas Layout: the whole window is the drawing; the tools, the settings and the job's lists float over it
tooltip-layout-rail = Rail Layout: a column of tool groups on the left, each opening its list of tools, and the settings on the right
tooltip-layout-ribbon = Ribbon Layout: tabs of tool groups across the top, the job's lists on the left and the settings on the right
tooltip-tile-windows-horizontal = Tile Horizontally: shows the 2D and 3D views together, one above the other
tooltip-tile-windows-vertical = Tile Vertically: shows the 2D and 3D views together, side by side
tooltip-cascade-windows = Cascade Windows: back to one view at a time, the 2D and 3D views on tabs
tooltip-auto-open-3d-view = Open 3D View Automatically: switches to the 3D view on its own each time a toolpath is calculated
tooltip-auto-wrapping-view = Wrapped View: shows a rotary job wrapped round its cylinder in the 3D view, as it will be cut
tooltip-animate-preview = Animate Preview: shows a toolpath preview being cut step by step, instead of all at once
tooltip-draw-2d-previews = Show Toolpaths in 2D: draws the selected toolpaths' cuts over the drawing in the 2D view
tooltip-make-2d-previews-solid = Solid 2D Previews: fills in the toolpaths drawn in the 2D view, to show how much material each one removes
tooltip-draw-rapid-moves = Show Rapid Moves: draws the fast moves the bit makes above the material between cuts
tooltip-draw-plunge-moves = Show Plunge Moves: draws the moves where the bit goes down into the material
tooltip-draw-retract-moves = Show Retract Moves: draws the moves where the bit lifts out of the material
tooltip-draw-join-moves = Show Join Moves: draws the short moves that link one cut to the next without lifting
tooltip-draw-material-block = Show Material Block: draws the block of material in the 3D view
tooltip-draw-modeling-plane = Show Modeling Plane: draws the flat plane the 3D model is built on in the 3D view
tooltip-draw-origin = Draw Origin: marks the job's zero point, where the machine's X, Y and Z start
tooltip-draw-vectors-in-3d-view = Show Vectors in 3D: draws the vectors over the model in the 3D view
tooltip-draw-keep-out-zones-in-3d-view = Show Keep-Out Zones in 3D: draws the areas the bit must stay out of, such as clamps, in the 3D view
tooltip-show-keep-out-zone-labels = Show Keep-Out Zone Labels: writes each keep-out zone's name on it in the views
tooltip-use-shaded-background = Shaded Background: fades the 3D view's background from light to dark instead of a plain colour
tooltip-use-shadow-shading = Shadows: shades the 3D view with shadows, so shallow carving is easier to see
tooltip-color-shaded-view = Colour Shaded View: shows the 3D model in its material's colour, wood with its grain, instead of plain grey
tooltip-light-follows-viewer = Light Follows Viewer: keeps the light behind you as you turn the 3D view, so the side facing you stays lit
tooltip-model-resolution-standard = Model Resolution Standard: the 3D model in normal detail, quickest to work with
tooltip-model-resolution-high = Model Resolution High: the 3D model in finer detail, about three times slower to work with
tooltip-model-resolution-highest = Model Resolution Highest: the 3D model in the finest detail, for small, detailed carvings; much slower
tooltip-reset-preview = Reset Preview: clears the preview back to uncut material; Undo Last Preview brings it back
tooltip-undo-last-preview = Undo Last Preview: goes back to the preview as it was before the last Preview or Reset Preview, once, turned over to the side the job is on now
tooltip-preview-quality-1 = Preview Quality Standard: moves the Preview detail slider to 20%, quick to work out; the preview showing is worked out again
tooltip-preview-quality-2 = Preview Quality High: moves the Preview detail slider to 40%; the preview showing is worked out again
tooltip-preview-quality-4 = Preview Quality Very High: moves the Preview detail slider to 60%; the preview showing is worked out again
tooltip-preview-quality-8 = Preview Quality Extremely High: moves the Preview detail slider to 80%; the preview showing is worked out again
tooltip-preview-quality-25 = Preview Quality Maximum: moves the Preview detail slider to 100%, the finest detail, for small bits and fine carving; the preview showing is worked out again
tooltip-create-component-from-toolpath-preview = Create Component from Toolpath Preview: turns the previewed, cut material into a 3D component, to carve on or reuse. It goes on the level of the component picked in the tree, else the top shown level, and the status bar names it
tooltip-segment-3d-model-file = Segment 3D Model File: splits a 3D model file into pieces thin enough for your material, to carve in layers
tooltip-machine-configuration = Machine Configuration: your machine's size, its post processor and the folder its files go to. If the saved machines can't be read at start, a copy is kept as machines.json.bad and they are never saved over
tooltip-add-machine = Add Machine: sets up another machine, with its size and the post processor that writes its G-code
tooltip-search-for-machine-online = Search for Machine Online: opens the list of ready-made machine set-ups in your browser
tooltip-install-offline-package = Install Offline Package: adds a machine set-up from a file you downloaded
tooltip-post-processor-management = Post Processor Management: the post processors, which write G-code in the form each kind of machine reads
tooltip-install-post-processor = Install Post Processor: adds a post processor file for a machine Cut Craft does not list yet. One with a name already listed is kept beside it as a copy, named with a copy number and the date and time
tooltip-job-sheet-editor = Job Setup Sheet Editor: chooses what the printed job sheet shows: the job, its bits and its toolpaths
tooltip-first-run-setup = First Run Setup: asks about your machine, units and material again, starting from your answers, and corrects My Machine (keeping the posts you added)
tooltip-options = Options: Cut Craft's settings, such as units, colours and where files are kept
tooltip-snap-options = Snap Options: chooses what the pointer snaps to as you draw: the grid, guides, ends, middles and centres
tooltip-keyboard-shortcuts = Keyboard Shortcuts: lists the keys that run each tool, so you can work without the menus
tooltip-help-contents = Help Contents: opens Cut Craft's help, with a page for every tool and a search box
tooltip-did-you-know = Did You Know?: short tips for getting more out of Cut Craft, one at a time
tooltip-back-up-settings = Back Up Settings: saves your settings, machines, bits and own files in one backup file, to keep safe or take to another computer
tooltip-check-for-updates = Check for Updates: asks straight away whether there is a newer version of Cut Craft
tooltip-about-cut-craft = About Cut Craft: its version, its licence and the people who made it
tooltip-credits = Credits: the libraries, pictures and icons Cut Craft is built with, and their licences
tooltip-open-application-data-folder = Open Application Data Folder: opens the folder where Cut Craft keeps your settings, bits and machines
tooltip-addons = Add-ons: installs, turns on and removes add-ons that bring new tools into Cut Craft. An add-on from GitHub never replaces Cut Craft's own add-ons or one installed from another repository. Remove asks first; a removed gadget leaves the Gadgets menu when Cut Craft restarts
tooltip-open-gadgets-folder = Open My Gadgets Folder: opens the folder where your own .lua gadget files go. Each one shows up in Gadgets ▸ My Gadgets when Cut Craft starts
tooltip-community-0 = GitHub: opens Cut Craft's page on GitHub, where you can report problems and see what is coming
tooltip-community-1 = Facebook: opens Facebook's home page in your browser
tooltip-community-2 = X: opens the X home page in your browser
tooltip-community-3 = YouTube: opens YouTube's home page in your browser
tooltip-community-4 = Instagram: opens Instagram's home page in your browser
tooltip-community-5 = Pinterest: opens Pinterest's home page in your browser, for project ideas
tooltip-community-6 = Thingiverse: opens Thingiverse's home page in your browser, for designs to download
tooltip-gadget-drill-grid = Drill Grid: draws rows and columns of circles in the middle of the job, for pegboards, shelf-pin holes and speaker grilles
tooltip-gadget-hole-pattern = Hole Pattern: draws circles spaced evenly round a circle in the middle of the job, for bolt circles and clock faces
tooltip-3d-finishing-toolpath = 3D Finishing Toolpath: a ball nose rasters over the model, as low as it can go at each point without cutting into it
tooltip-3d-pencil-toolpath = 3D Pencil Toolpath: a small ball nose runs along the valleys and inside corners of the model, where the bigger bit that finished it was too round to reach, and cleans out what it left there
tooltip-3d-roughing-toolpath = 3D Roughing Toolpath: an end mill clears the material above the model level by level, leaving an allowance for the finishing toolpath: flat at each level (Z level), or riding over the model a pass depth at a time (3D raster)
tooltip-activate-sheet = Activate Sheet: work on another sheet; the job takes its setup
tooltip-add-draft = Add Draft to Model: a new component holding the visible model with no wall steeper than the draft angle allows (material is added at the foot of steep walls), for moulds
tooltip-add-layer = Add Layer: a new layer on top, made current so new vectors go on it
tooltip-add-sheet = Add New Sheet: another material sheet, sized as the one it was asked from (the sheet right-clicked) or else as the active one, which stays active
tooltip-add-zero-plane = Add Zero Plane: a flat component at height 0 over the whole material, a base for others
tooltip-array-copy = Array Copy: a grid of copies of the selected vectors, above and to the right of them, each mirrored or turned in a repeating block (symmetry), every other row or column moved along (displacement), and if asked all grouped
tooltip-array-copy-toolpath = Array Copy Toolpath: a grid of copies of the toolpaths shown in the toolpath list when Apply is pressed (tick the ones to copy there), above and to the right of them, kept up to date with them: recalculating copies them again
tooltip-auto-layout-text = Auto Layout Text: the words wrapped into as many lines as make them biggest, scaled to fill the selected closed vector inside a border, and grouped so they pick and move as one
tooltip-bake-components = Bake Components: the visible components replaced by one holding the model they make, with shape only where they had it (its outline, for a Model Boundary or Create Vector Boundary, is theirs, not the whole job)
tooltip-bitmap-properties = Bitmap Properties: a picture's name, position and size on the job
tooltip-celtic-weave = Celtic Weave Creator: a Celtic knot's loops as smooth closed vectors, the drive rails Extrude and Weave turns into a weave
tooltip-chamfer-toolpath = Chamfer Toolpath: a sloped edge along the selected shapes, inside or outside them and sloping down or up away from them
tooltip-circular-copy = Circular Copy: copies of the selected vectors spaced evenly round a centre
tooltip-close-extend-vector = Close / Extend Vector: closes the selected open vectors, with a straight line from end to start or by extending their end lines until they meet
tooltip-close-with-line = Close With a Line: the open vector under the point is closed by a straight line from its end back to its start
tooltip-component-boundary = Create Vector Boundary Around Selected Components: closed vectors round the silhouette of the selected components (all visible ones when none is selected), grouped when there are several, for use as toolpath boundaries
tooltip-component-properties = Component Properties: a component's name, how it combines with the model under it, whether it is part of the model, and its dynamic shape and base height, fade and tilt (kept apart from its heights until baked)
tooltip-make-construction-line = Make Construction Line: turns the selected vectors into construction lines, drawn dashed, that place things (Embellish along them, bend a drawing along them, snap to them) but are never cut and never exported
tooltip-convert-text-to-curves = Convert Text to Curves: the selected text becomes plain vectors that node editing can change, still grouped; after it, the text cannot be edited as text
tooltip-copy-along-vectors = Copy Along Vectors: copies of an object spaced along vectors
tooltip-copy-to-other-side = Copy to Other Side: in a double-sided job, the selected vectors copied onto the other side, mirrored as the material is turned over so they line up through it (right-click ▸ Copy to ▸ Other Side)
tooltip-copy-toolpath-to-sheet = Copy Toolpath to Sheet: a toolpath onto another sheet, with copies of the vectors it was made from, so it can be recalculated there
tooltip-create-component-from-bitmap = Create Component from Bitmap: the newest picture as a relief, its tones as heights (a depth map's at full precision, so a 16-bit or floating point one does not terrace)
tooltip-create-component-from-visible-model = Create Component from Visible Model: a new component holding the model the visible components make, with shape only where they have it; they are hidden, so the model looks the same
tooltip-create-fillets = Create Fillets: rounds the sharp corners of the selected vectors, cuts dog-bone or T-bone relief into them so a round cutter can clear the corner fully, or loops a plasma or drag knife round the outside of them
tooltip-create-shape = Create Shape: a 3D component raised over the selected closed vectors, rising from their edges as a round dome, an angled slope, an S, a flat top, or (Custom) the profile of an open vector selected with them
tooltip-crop-bitmap = Crop Bitmap: trims the selected picture to the selected closed vectors, everything outside them cleared to white
tooltip-cross-section = Create Cross Section Vector: an open vector of the visible model's profile along a line dragged across it, drawn from the line's start with distance along the line across and the model's height up (1:1)
tooltip-cut-vector = Cut Vector: the vector is cut open at the node under the point (an open one in two)
tooltip-decorative-relief = Create Decorative Relief: the baroque or western-leaf scrolls of Create Vector Texture raised as a 3D component inside the selected closed vectors (or the job): rounded bands rolling into raised eyes, lobed leaves lying over them and curling up towards their tips, domed flowers, ready for 3D roughing and finishing
tooltip-delete = Delete: removes the selected vectors, text and pictures from the job
tooltip-delete-component = Delete Component: removes a 3D component from the model
tooltip-delete-items = Delete Items: the right-click delete family (This, Visible, Invisible, Empty, All) for layers, toolpaths or components, built from each kind's delete command
tooltip-delete-layer = Delete Layer: removes a layer and every vector on it
tooltip-delete-level = Delete Level: a level and the components on it; a job keeps at least one level
tooltip-delete-point = Delete Point: the node under the point goes; its spans become one line
tooltip-delete-sheet = Delete Sheet: removes a sheet and what is on it; a job keeps at least one
tooltip-delete-toolpath = Delete Toolpath: removes a toolpath from the toolpath list
tooltip-dimensions = Dimensions: a length, horizontal or vertical dimension between two points, an angle at a corner or an arc's radius or diameter, as vectors: extension lines, a dimension line with arrow heads, and the measurement in a font, grouped
tooltip-distort-object = Distort Object: the selected vectors, or the selected components, bent into an envelope: their bounding box with its corners moved, the band above an open curve, or the band between two open curves (the last one or two vectors picked)
tooltip-document-variables = Document Variables: named values kept with the job, used in number fields' sums as `{"{"}name{"}"}`
tooltip-drag-knife-toolpath = Drag Knife Toolpath: a trailing blade cuts along the selected vectors
tooltip-draw-arc = Draw Arc: counter-clockwise from the start angle to the end angle
tooltip-draw-circle = Draw Circle: drag from the centre out to the edge, or type the centre and radius
tooltip-draw-curve = Draw Curve: a smooth curve through a list of points, as Béziers whose tangent at each point runs parallel to its neighbours (a Catmull-Rom spline)
tooltip-draw-ellipse = Draw Ellipse: an oval, dragged from its centre out to a corner of the box it fits, or typed as a centre, width and height
tooltip-draw-freehand = Draw Freehand: the pointer's path while dragging, smoothed into Béziers
tooltip-draw-polygon = Draw Polygon: a regular polygon with its first vertex straight up (before rotation)
tooltip-draw-polyline = Draw Line / Polyline: lines through a list of points, each span straight or (drawn with a drag in the 2D view) a smooth curve
tooltip-draw-rectangle = Draw Rectangle: drag from one corner to the opposite one, or type its position and size
tooltip-draw-star = Draw Star: alternating outer and inner vertices, first point straight up (before rotation)
tooltip-draw-text = Draw Text: the words as vectors in a TrueType or single-line font, grouped so they pick and move as one
tooltip-drill-bank-toolpath = Drill Bank Toolpath: the selected circles drilled by the machine's drill bank, as many at once as line up with its drills
tooltip-drilling-toolpath = Drilling Toolpath: a hole at the centre of each selected closed vector, straight down or pecked a pass depth at a time, retracting above the start or above the last peck, and dwelling at the bottom of each peck if asked (the post needs a `DWELL_MOVE` block)
tooltip-duplicate-component = Duplicate Component: a copy of a component, in the same place on the same level, just above it in the tree (the top of the tree, as new components go)
tooltip-duplicate-toolpath = Duplicate Toolpath: a copy added to the toolpath list, named with the next free number after it ("Cut out (1)")
tooltip-edit-picture = Edit Picture: a picture's contrast, brightness and gamma, inverted if asked, and a border that fades its edges to white
tooltip-embellish = Embellish: ornament designed for the selected shape or line rather than cut out of a pattern
tooltip-emboss = Emboss Component: the selected component made much lower while its surface detail stays: its broad shape (a blur of it) is scaled to the new height, the detail on top of that is kept, then smoothed
tooltip-engrave-part-names = Engrave Part Names: each part's number and name drawn as text in the middle of the part, on a "Part Names" layer, so a Quick Engrave or V-Carve toolpath from that layer marks every part with what its label says
tooltip-extrude-and-weave = Extrude and Weave: a shape swept along drive rails
tooltip-fit-curves-to-vectors = Fit Curves to Vectors: the selected vectors redrawn as circular arcs, Béziers or straight lines within a tolerance, replacing them on their own layer or added beside them on the current layer
tooltip-fluting-toolpath = Fluting Toolpath: cuts along the selected vectors from their start points, ramping the depth so the cut tapers in (and out), as for decorative flutes
tooltip-generate-border = Generate Border: one repeating length of picture-frame moulding in a style you pick, made by the Borders add-on with your own Google key and saved to your Library under Generated ▸ Borders as a depth map with its photo, ready to place like any 3D model
tooltip-group = Group: the selected objects become one group, picked and moved together (dragging any one of them, picked or not, moves the whole group)
tooltip-group-components = Group Components: the selected components (two or more, on one level) made one group of the tree
tooltip-group-properties = Group Properties: a component group's name and how it combines with what is under it, set on every member
tooltip-import-toolpaths = Import Toolpaths: a G-code file (as a post-processor writes it, from Cut Craft or another program) read back as toolpaths, one for each bit it uses, to preview, check and save again through another post
tooltip-inlay-toolpath = Inlay Toolpath: a part and the cavity it fits, cut with one bit
tooltip-insert-level = Insert New Level: an empty level on top of the component tree
tooltip-insert-point = Insert Point: a new node on the span under the point, splitting it there
tooltip-interactive-vector-trim = Interactive Vector Trim: click a piece of a vector and the stretch between the nearest crossings with other vectors either side of the click is cut away; drag across pieces and every piece the drag crosses goes
tooltip-job-setup = Job Setup: the material block, where the machine's zero is on it, how finely the model is worked out and how the material looks
tooltip-join-close-vectors = Join / Close Vectors: open vectors joined end to end, or an open one closed, with a straight line, a smooth curve or by moving the end points together
tooltip-join-open-ends = Join Open Ends: click the end of an open vector, then the end it should meet, and the two are joined there with a straight line, by running both ends on until they meet, or with arcs that carry on smoothly from each end
tooltip-join-vectors = Join Vectors: joins selected open vectors whose ends lie close together into one longer vector, closing it when its ends meet
tooltip-keep-out-zones = Keep-Out Zones: areas a bit must not pass over, made from the selected closed vectors grown by a clearance, or cleared
tooltip-keyhole-toolpath = Keyhole Toolpath: hanging slots on the back of a sign
tooltip-laser-cut-fill-toolpath = Laser Cut / Fill: a laser cuts round the selected shapes, allowing for its kerf, or marks them with a hatched fill
tooltip-laser-picture-toolpath = Laser Picture: a laser burns a picture in lines across it, its power following how dark the picture is, or (dithered) switching full on and off to give the tones
tooltip-layer-properties = Layer Properties: changes a layer's name, whether it is shown or locked against changes, the material its vectors are cut from, and the colour they are drawn in
tooltip-level-clipping = Level Clipping: a level kept only inside the selected closed vectors, without changing its components
tooltip-level-properties = Level Properties: a level's name, how it combines with the levels below, whether it is part of the model, its base height, mirror mode and (rotary jobs) wrapping
tooltip-make-start-point = Make Start Point: the closed vector starts at the node under the point
tooltip-material-setup = Material Setup (opened before the first toolpath): the material's thickness, Z zero, XY datum, rapid Z gaps and home, as in Job Setup, and where the 3D model sits in the material, by the gap above its top (Gap Outside Model on rotary jobs) or below its bottom (Gap Inside Model, from the axis), with the model's thickness, which Set scales
tooltip-materials = Preview Colors: how the 3D view and the toolpath preview colour the job, and nothing else: feeds and speeds come from Job Setup's Material
tooltip-merged-toolpath = Merged Toolpath: the toolpaths shown in the toolpath list when Apply is pressed (tick the ones to merge there), all using one bit, made into one, with their cuts in whichever of the orders asked for leaves the least travelling between them, each part's cuts together when asked; and Ungroup, which takes a merged toolpath apart again
tooltip-mirror = Mirror (Mirror Selected Objects): flips the selection in place, about the job's centre, or beside itself (to the left, right, top or bottom), or about the line between the ends of the vector picked last; or leaves the selection and adds mirrored copies
tooltip-moulding-toolpath = Moulding Toolpath: sweeps an open cross-section profile along drive rails, cutting the moulding in passes parallel to the rails, each as low as the bit can go without cutting into the profile
tooltip-move = Move: the selection to a point (an anchor of its box there), or by an offset, which (relative rotated) can be turned by an angle to follow work laid out at that angle
tooltip-move-nodes = Move Nodes: the nodes picked with a box while node editing move together by one offset
tooltip-move-to-layer = Move to Layer: puts the selected vectors on another layer, to show, hide or machine them with that layer's other vectors
tooltip-move-to-level = Move to Level: moves the selected 3D components onto another level of the model, which changes how they combine with the rest
tooltip-name-part = Name Part: gives the selected parts a name, which the cut list and the part labels print
tooltip-nest-parts = Nest Parts: the selected vectors, as parts (vectors whose boxes overlap, or that are grouped, stay together), laid out inside the job from a chosen corner, kept a bit's width plus a clearance apart and a border in from the edge: by their boxes in rows, or (True Shape) each where its own shape first fits, turned in steps, holes filled by smaller parts, with as many copies of each as asked; mirrored where that fits better, inside a boundary layer's vectors, onto new sheets when the job is full, with a double- sided part's other side following it, and filler parts in what is left
tooltip-notes = Notes: rich text kept with the job (headings, lists, check boxes, links, bold and italic, never HTML) with live variables (see [`cut_craft_core::notes`])
tooltip-offset-model = Offset Model: a new component holding the visible model grown (or shrunk) by a ball of the offset's radius in 3D; the components it came from are hidden
tooltip-offset-vectors = Offset Vectors: draws a copy of each selected vector a set distance outside or inside it, for a border, an inlay or a frame
tooltip-orientate-3d-model = Orientate 3D Model: stand a 3D model the right way up, size it and place it in the material before it becomes a component
tooltip-overlap-intersect = Overlap: replaces the selected closed shapes with only the part where they all overlap
tooltip-photo-vcarve-toolpath = Photo V-Carve Toolpath (V-bit carved photo): a V-bit etches a picture as grooves, deeper (so wider) where it is darker, along parallel lines across it or along the selected vectors
tooltip-plate-production = Plate Production: badges or nameplates from a template and a data file
tooltip-pocket-toolpath = Pocket Toolpath: clears the inside of the selected closed vectors at each depth, with rings that step in from the outline (worked from the middle outwards), with raster lines and a profile pass round the edge, or adaptively, the bit keeping a thin, steady bite everywhere so it never cuts with more than a sliver of its edge
tooltip-prism-toolpath = Prism Carving Toolpath: a V-bit runs along the edges of the selected shapes deep enough that its sloping sides leave each shape standing as a raised, ridged bevel
tooltip-profile-toolpath = Profile Toolpath: cuts along the selected vectors, outside, inside or on the line
tooltip-quick-engrave-toolpath = Quick Engrave: marks the selected vectors at a shallow depth, along their lines or filling them with an offset, hatch or cross hatch pattern
tooltip-quick-trace = Quick Trace: traces the chosen picture into vectors in one click, with settings picked to suit it
tooltip-relief-from-photo = Relief from Photo: a photo whose depth has been estimated (the Depth add-on fills the picture's depth) shaped into a relief: the backdrop cut away, the subject lifted clear of it, fine detail from the photo's shading added back and the noise smoothed
tooltip-reorder-component = Move Component (the component tree's blue arrows): a component one place up or down among those on its level
tooltip-reorder-layer = Move Layer (the Layers List's arrows): a layer one place up or down the list, the order the layers are listed and drawn in
tooltip-reorder-level = Move Level: a level one place up or down the component tree
tooltip-reorder-toolpath = Move Toolpath (the toolpath list's up and down arrows): a toolpath one place up or down the list, which is the order it is cut and saved in
tooltip-replace-below = Replace Below: the parts of the selected component lower than a height are removed or flattened to it, and the component can be lowered by that height
tooltip-reset-inside-selected-vectors = Reset Inside Selected Vectors: clears the shape inside the selected closed vectors, so the model there is back to the flat base: only on the components picked, or on every shown one when none is picked
tooltip-reset-outside-selected-vectors = Reset Outside Selected Vectors: clears the shape outside the selected closed vectors, so the model there is back to the flat base: only on the components picked, or on every shown one when none is picked
tooltip-reverse-direction = Reverse Direction: the vector under the point runs the other way
tooltip-rotary-details-toolpath = Rotary Details: on a rotary job, a smaller bit after the finish, cutting only what the bigger bits before it could not reach: the grooves, corners and fine detail they left
tooltip-rotary-finishing-toolpath = Rotary Finishing: the last pass over a carved part on a rotary job, the bit kept on the model all the way round, as low as it goes without touching it
tooltip-rotary-lathe-toolpath = Rotary Lathe: on a rotary job, A spins the material steadily while the bit stays straight over the turning axis and steps down, as on a lathe: to face an end, to turn the part round to its outline, or to part it off
tooltip-rotary-locked-angles-toolpath = Rotary Locked Angles: on a rotary job, A turns to an angle and locks there while the bit finishes the side facing it back and forth along the part, like a flat 3D finish; then the next angle, and the next
tooltip-rotary-machining-toolpath = 4-Axis Rotary Machining: finishes a model all the way round a turning cylinder, ring by ring, the bit kept on the true round surface: X (or Y), Z and A move together
tooltip-rotary-roughing-toolpath = Rotary Roughing: takes the bulk off a carved part on a rotary job, a level at a time from the outside in, all the way round at each level before the next, down to the allowance left on the model for the finish
tooltip-rotate = Rotate: turns the selected objects by an angle, about a point of their box
tooltip-rounding-toolpath = Rounding Toolpath: on a rotary job, turns a square or round blank down to the job's diameter in levels, either round the cylinder or along it
tooltip-scale-model-z-height = Scale Model Z Height: stretches or squashes the model to a new height, scaling every visible component's heights, base heights and tilts, and the shown levels' base heights, by the same factor
tooltip-sculpt = Sculpting: a brush dragged over the selected component (several are baked into one) smooths, smudges, adds or removes height, or brings back the shape it had before sculpting
tooltip-segment-3d-model = Segment 3D Model: an STL split by planes square to one axis into segments, so a model with undercuts can be machined in pieces on a 3-axis machine: one cut where asked, or several in equal slices
tooltip-select-layer-vectors = Select Vectors on Layer: selects every vector on one layer, to move, edit or machine them together
tooltip-send-to-sheet = Copy / Move to Sheet: the selected vectors onto another sheet, each keeping its layer and group; moving takes them off this one
tooltip-set-current-layer = Set Current Layer: picks the layer you are working on
tooltip-set-size = Set Size: the selection, or each selected item on its own, sized to a width and height (in millimetres, or as a percentage of the size it has), about an anchor point
tooltip-sheet-properties = Sheet Properties: renames a sheet, the name shown for it in the Sheets list
tooltip-show-hide = Show / Hide: the right-click visibility family (Show This, Show Only This, Show All But This, Show All, Hide This, Hide All) for layers, toolpaths or components, built from each kind's properties command
tooltip-sketch-carving-toolpath = Sketch Carving Toolpath: carves the lines of a sketch drawn from a picture or the 3D model: wherever it is darker (or lower) than its surroundings
tooltip-slice = Slice Model: the visible model divided into Z bands, each a new component starting at the zero plane, for parts thicker than the material or the machine allows
tooltip-smooth-point = Smooth Point (node editing's right-click): the node under the point becomes smooth, its two spans Béziers whose handles there lie on one line
tooltip-smooth-selected-components = Smooth Selected Components: softens the shape of each component picked in the component tree (the newest when none is) by averaging each height with its neighbours, once per pass
tooltip-space-horizontally = Space Horizontally: evenly spaces the selected objects along x, the outermost staying put
tooltip-space-vertically = Space Vertically: evenly spaces the selected objects along y, the outermost staying put
tooltip-split = Split Component: the selected component cut in two by a selected closed vector, as a cookie cutter would: "- A" inside, "- B" outside
tooltip-subtract-vectors = Subtract Vectors: cuts the other selected closed shapes out of the largest one, like a cookie cutter
tooltip-surfacing-toolpath = Surfacing Toolpath: flattens the whole material, the spoilboard, or a shape with a wide surfacing bit, in rows or a spiral that run past every edge
tooltip-swap-sides = Swap Sides: in a double-sided job, work on the other side of the material
tooltip-text-on-a-curve = Text on a Curve: one line of selected text (made with Draw Text) and a selected curve; the letters are laid along the curve, above, on or below it, turned with it or upright
tooltip-texture-area = Create Texture Area: the component picked in the component tree tiled over the selected closed vectors (or the whole job) with spacing, alternate-row and -column shifts and reflections in each group of four, as one new component; the tile is hidden
tooltip-texture-toolpath = Texture Toolpath: rows of shallow scallops of random depth and length, as a hand-tooled finish, inside the selected shapes; or the selected vectors themselves cut at random depths
tooltip-thread-milling-toolpath = Thread Milling Toolpath: a single-point thread mill spirals round the centre of each selected vector, cutting an internal thread (a nut) or an external one (a bolt)
tooltip-toolpath-properties = Toolpath Properties: a toolpath's name, whether it is shown and previewed, and its colour in a Toolpath Color preview
tooltip-toolpath-tiling = Toolpath Tiling: save the toolpaths in tiles for a machine smaller than the job
tooltip-trace-bitmap = Trace Bitmap: closed vectors round the dark (or light) regions of the chosen bitmap, fitted with arcs, for machining a picture's shapes
tooltip-trim-objects = Trim Objects (Trim selected objects to last selected objects): every selected vector is cut where it crosses the closed vector picked last (and the rest of its group), and the pieces inside it, or outside it, are cleared away
tooltip-turn-and-spin = Turn and Spin: a component from an open profile vector, turned round the line from its start to its end (a lathe shape) or spun round its left end point (a dish or dome)
tooltip-two-rail-sweep = Two Rail Sweep: open cross-sections swept between two rails, stretched across the gap between them all the way along
tooltip-ungroup = Ungroup: the selected groups come apart one level, onto the layers their vectors are on (grouping never moves them), or all onto the current layer
tooltip-ungroup-components = Ungroup Components: the group of the chosen component taken apart, its members left as lone components where they are
tooltip-vcarve-engrave-toolpath = V-Carve / Engrave Toolpath (V-bit carving): a V-bit carves the selected shapes, going deeper the further it is from their edges so its sides cut the edges exactly
tooltip-vcarve-inlay-toolpath = V-Carve Inlay Toolpath (V-bit carved inlay): two V-carvings that fit together
tooltip-vector-boundary = Vector Boundary: closed boundaries round the selected vectors
tooltip-vector-selector = Vector Selector: selects the vectors that pass its filters (open, closed, circles, circles of a diameter) on every visible layer, the current one, or the layers named; the filters live in `cut_craft_core::selector`, where toolpaths use them too
tooltip-vector-texture = Create Vector Texture: rows of wavy lines at an angle over the selected closed vectors (or the job), their spacing, waves and noise varied by a seeded pattern; or one of the decorative fills (floral vines, baroque scrolls, frost, snowflakes, fractal branches, stones, ripples, hammered dimples) grown inside them, every line kept a carvable gap from the others and from the edge
tooltip-vector-unwrapper = Vector Unwrapper (rotary jobs): a closed cross-section of the turned shape becomes the open profile Two Rail Sweep needs
tooltip-vector-validator = Vector Validator: finds vectors that would stop toolpaths being made (overlapping, crossing themselves or each other, or with zero-length spans) and selects them, or fixes the zero-length spans
tooltip-weld-vectors = Weld Vectors: merges overlapping closed shapes into one outline, the lines inside them taken away
tooltip-wrapped-fluting-layout = Wrapped Fluting Layout: on a rotary job's unrolled surface, flutes along the axis evenly spaced round the cylinder, and coves round it at either end if asked
tooltip-wrapped-spiral-layout = Wrapped Spiral Layout: rope or barley-twist strands on a rotary job's unrolled surface
tooltip-machine-files = See the files on the machine's card or shared folder, and upload, rename, delete or make folders there, without walking over to the machine
tooltip-import-vectors-bitmap = Bring in a drawing (DXF, SVG or a Vectric job's vectors) or a picture (PNG, JPG, BMP, GIF or TIFF) to trace, carve round or draw over. An SVG sized in pixels is read at 96 pixels per inch, and a note says the size it came in at
tooltip-import-vectors = Bring in a drawing made in another program: DXF, SVG or a Vectric job's vectors
tooltip-import-into-shape = Select a closed shape first (a circle, plaque or heart), then bring in a drawing or picture sized to fit inside it: scaled, stretched or bent to follow its outline. Select an open line instead to bend the drawing along it, like lettering on an arc
tooltip-import-component-3d-model = Bring in a 3D model (STL or OBJ) or saved 3D clipart, to size, place and carve
tooltip-clipart-library = Open the Library tab: your folders of ready-made drawings, pictures and 3D clipart, to drag onto the job
tooltip-import-toolpaths-file = Read a G-code file (.nc, .tap, .gcode and the like) back in as toolpaths, to preview and check it before it runs
tooltip-import-cut-list = Draw a part for each row of a spreadsheet's cut list (saved as CSV): name, length, width and how many, ready for Nest Parts. Sizes are in the units after the Length and Width headings, such as Length (in) or Length (mm), else in the job's units. The note after importing names the units used for each, so a heading missing its unit shows up
tooltip-export-as-stl = Save the 3D model as an STL file, for a 3D printer or another program
tooltip-export-as-grayscale-bitmap = Save the 3D model as a PNG picture where lighter is higher, for another carving program
tooltip-export-as-3d-clipart = Save the selected 3D parts as clipart, to drop into other jobs from the Library
tooltip-load-template = Add the toolpaths saved in a template to this job, ready to pick the vectors (or picture) each one cuts and calculate. A Merged or Array Copy toolpath uses the toolpaths saved with it; one saved without them says to tick the ones to use
tooltip-save-selected-toolpath-as-template = Save the selected toolpath's settings and bits, to make the same cut on another job
tooltip-save-all-visible-toolpaths-as-template = Save the settings and tools of every toolpath shown in the list, to make the same cuts on another job
tooltip-create-job-sheet = Save a page for the machine: the job, the material, each toolpath's bit and how long it takes
tooltip-print-job-sheet = Open the job sheet in the web browser to print it: the job, the material, each toolpath's bit and how long it takes
tooltip-part-labels = Print a label for each named part, to stick on it once it is cut out
tooltip-clearing-settings = How adaptive and trochoidal clearing cut in this job: the light step, the loops, and whether rows and loops keep climb on the way back
tooltip-advanced-rotary-mode = Open Options at Advanced rotary mode: each rotary toolpath then cuts the whole blank, not only what the toolpaths above it leave
tooltip-cut-list = Save a list of the job's parts and their sizes, as a spreadsheet (CSV)
tooltip-show-open-vector-ends = Put a circle on each end of every open vector, so a gap that stops a shape being pocketed or carved stands out
tooltip-show-construction-lines = Show or hide the dashed construction lines: lines that only place things and are never cut. Hidden, they cannot be picked either
tooltip-draw-rectangle-from-center = Draw Rectangle from Center: drag from the middle out to a corner
tooltip-draw-circle-from-edge = Draw Circle from Edge: drag from one side straight across to the other
